1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,295
I'm Jack Thompson, presenting another edition of “Tips for Your Trip”.

2
00:00:05,315 --> 00:00:12,375
Christmas time is here again, so it's important for all of you making that long drive home to be extra careful on the road.

3
00:00:12,975 --> 00:00:13,895
So listen carefully.

4
00:00:14,735 --> 00:00:20,935
Firstly, there will be many tired and stressed drivers on the road, so you will need to be extra careful.

5
00:00:21,615 --> 00:00:26,435
Secondly, try to share the driving with a friend or relative or two if possible.

6
00:00:26,435 --> 00:00:39,835
That way there will always be someone who can take over the steering wheel when you're tired.Thirdly, take a break when you start to notice the effects of drowsiness—drifting, blurry vision, and yawning.

7
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:46,660
And finally, remember that drinking a lot of coffee can only help you fight drowsiness for a short time.

8
00:00:47,115 --> 00:00:50,375
Learn to recognize the signs of sleepiness, and stop.

9
00:00:50,835 --> 00:00:51,735
Have a good sleep.

10
00:00:52,315 --> 00:00:55,250
Don't drive after midnight if you can possibly avoid it.

11
00:00:55,660 --> 00:01:00,455
That's all, but please listen again next week for more“Tips for Your Trip”.
